{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"advisory":[{"block_threshold":0.5,"blocking_enabled":true,"carried_from":"1","criteria":["error-handling"],"decision":"advisory","evidence":["scripts/cast_gerrit_verified_vote.py:50: `return _CLOSED_CHANGE_NEEDLE in f\"{completed.stderr}\\n{completed.stdout}\"`","scripts/cast_gerrit_verified_vote.py:111: `if completed.returncode != 0 and _is_closed_change_error(completed):`","The guard is gated on returncode != 0 and only downgrades a specific string, so genuinely unrelated failures (e.g. ssh 255 host-key errors) still fail closed; the residual concern is only that the needle is a plain substring of merged output."],"finding":"The closed-change classifier matches the needle against combined stderr+stdout for ANY nonzero return, but does not require that the Gerrit review command actually ran to completion — an ssh transport that returns nonzero while somehow surfacing the needle text from an unrelated source would be treated as a benign no-op. In practice the needle is Gerrit-emitted, so this is low risk, but the guard trusts substring presence rather than a Gerrit-produced-output signal.","id":"2","impact":0.0,"location":"scripts/cast_gerrit_verified_vote.py:49","norm_id":"n40a01f88388cda3d","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","standing":{"origin_decision":"advisory","origin_revision":"2e8d2a35390e22ac9928b2a2d02e7c73c7b1e02f","state":"still-present"},"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8571,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes",